  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: mysql:8.4 security update",
  "description": "A security update for MySQL 8.4 addresses multiple vulnerabilities including system takeover, unauthorized server takeover, unauthorized data modification, and numerous denial of service (DoS) flaws across various components such as InnoDB, Server Optimizer, replication, client programs, and plugins. These vulnerabilities could allow attackers to compromise server integrity, cause service disruptions, or modify data without authorization. The update is rated as important by Red Hat and affects Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9 across multiple architectures.",
